px solid var(--rule)">about 18 min</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 23 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 15 min</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">North Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 15 min</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">Pawleys Island</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 13 min</td><td style="padding:.6rem .5rem;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">about 18 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem;margin-top:1.1rem">The differences come from the roads, not the distance. Ten miles on US-17 through the beach towns runs slower because of the traffic lights. Ten miles on SC-31 or SC-22 runs quicker because there are almost none, and that is the route locals take all summer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On season adds about five minutes to a ten mile drive. That is what our team plans on from driving these roads, not a measurement. Summer weekends on US-17 are the exception and run longer than that.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">If you will be working here, measure your own commute before you offer. The freeways, the two US 17s and the airport are on our <a href="/buyers/re