use our data source does not measure it. That is not the same as no demand. It sits beside the new Carolina Forest hospital, and a furnished monthly rental there serves traveling nurses on 13-week contracts. <a href="/invest/mid-term-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Furnished monthly rentals</a> covers that, and <a href="/invest/where-to-buy/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">where to buy</a> has the nightly-rental rules, which ban them in most neighborhoods.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-area-is-best-for-each-number"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Which area is best for each number?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hover an area, or tap it, for its numbers. The buttons change what the color shows. Darker is higher.</p>
